  "description": "Epoched, artifact-screened intracranial EEG from adults with drug-resistant epilepsy performing an auditory perceptual threshold task. A 75 ms target sound was embedded in white noise at each participant's 50% detection threshold, and trials are sorted into Perceived, Not Perceived and blank categories. The derivative release repackages the authors' 2-s grey-matter-electrode epochs from 30 participants (32 recordings) into BIDS; the continuous recordings were not released.",
  "methods_description": "Participants with subdural grid, strip and depth electrodes at Yale New Haven Hospital, Northwell Health and Mount Sinai reported whether they heard a target sound and which one it was. Trials were epoched around the target and screened visually for epileptic events. A four-stage artifact rejection followed, and only grey-matter electrodes were kept. Removed channel-epochs are stored as NaN. The data are stored as BrainVision IEEE float32 files, one per participant and implantation, with epochs concatenated and marked in events.tsv.",
